### Rotating Card – CSS + HTML

Below is a minimal example that shows a card (a `div` with some content) that rotates 180 degrees around its Y‑axis when you hover over it.  
Feel free to adjust the size, colors, or animation duration to fit your design.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card</title>
<style>
/* Container that keeps the card centered */
.card-wrapper {
  perspective: 1000px;          /* Gives depth to the 3D effect */
  width: 300px;
  height: 200px;
  margin: 50px auto;            /* Center horizontally */
}

/* The card itself */
.card {
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  background: #fff;
  border-radius: 12px;
  box-shadow: 0 10px 20px rgba(0,0,0,.2);
  transition: transform 0.6s ease;   /* Smooth rotation */
  transform-style: preserve-3d;      /* Needed for 3D transforms */
  position: relative;
}

/* Front side of the card */
.card .front,
.card .back {
  backface-visibility: hidden;     /* Hide the reverse side while rotating */
  position: absolute;
  top: 0;
  left: 0;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  border-radius: 12px;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
  font-size: 1.2rem;
  color: #333;
}

/* Back side – rotated 180° so it starts hidden */
.card .back {
  transform: rotateY(180deg);
  background: #f8f8f8;
}

/* Hover effect – flip the card */
.card:hover {
  transform: rotateY(180deg);
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="card-wrapper">
  <div class="card">
    <!-- Front side -->
    <div class="front">
      <p>Front Side</p>
    </div>
    <!-- Back side -->
    <div class="back">
      <p>Back Side</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

#### How it works

| Element | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `.card-wrapper` | Provides a 3D perspective so the rotation looks realistic. |
| `.card` | Holds both sides and defines the transition. |
| `.front` / `.back` | Each side of the card. `backface-visibility: hidden` hides the side that is turned away from the viewer. |
| `transform: rotateY(180deg)` on `.back` | Positions the back side behind the front. |
| `transform: rotateY(180deg)` on `.card:hover` | Flips the whole card when hovered. |

You can replace the `<p>` tags with images, icons, or any other content you like. Just keep the same structure and the rotation will work automatically.
